WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:01.973
- Education.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.023
To me, education is it.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.560
If you don't know how to
read, if you don't know

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.960
how to write, if you
don't know how to spell

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.063
then life is tough.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.330
And people having real problems

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.600
in these different neighborhoods.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.670
You're gonna feed your
kids or you're gonna

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.420
go to school; you're gonna pay your rent

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.610
or you're gonna go to
school, and I understand that

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:24.760
'cause I've been there.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.490
But I want people to know that
the bus represents change,

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.490
change in self, change in community,

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.283
change in everything.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.430
I want them to see that this
bus is something different

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.033
and anything is possible.

00:00:42.301 --> 00:00:44.718
(calm music)

00:00:54.941 --> 00:00:58.024
(somber piano music)

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:04.723
I grew up in Sunnydale
projects in San Francisco.

00:01:06.045 --> 00:01:08.240
It was just me and my
brother and my sister,

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.743
my mother had to work a
lot, she did overnights.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.861
This a really rough
neighborhood, and as I grew up,

00:01:15.861 --> 00:01:19.140
a lot of people started
fighting, selling drugs,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.500
doing drugs, so I started
selling drugs and robbery,

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.250
prostitution, and dropped out of school

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:27.550
to do what I wanted to do.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.377
Then one day, my son, he asked me,

00:01:31.377 --> 00:01:34.590
"You didn't go to school,
why I gotta go to school?"

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.523
So I started thinking
about changing my life.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:41.190
I went to a lady who's in our community

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:44.117
and she said, "There's a
program coming called Five Keys.

00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:46.127
"You can learn how to
read and get your GED

00:01:46.127 --> 00:01:48.220
"or your high school diploma."

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.870
It was like everything just
started falling in place.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.340
From that point, I started
going, going, going, going

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.740
until I learned how to read.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.030
I graduated in 2015,

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.830
had the cap and gown, I walked down,

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.960
they played the little music,

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:08.060
it was almost the happiest day of my life.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.220
And I said OK, now that I graduated,

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.190
I got my high school
diploma, can I get a job?

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.650
And they made a position for me;

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:18.250
that's what I am now,
the Community Ambassador;

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.050
and so now I'm giving back
and I'm helping other people.

00:02:34.685 --> 00:02:38.760
Five Keys' mobile classroom
is a classroom on wheels.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:41.570
It's a bus that drives up
to different neighborhoods,

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.360
different projects, and
we spend about three hours

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.083
in each neighborhood.

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:46.916
- Yes!

00:02:49.537 --> 00:02:51.498
- Happy to see you.

00:02:51.498 --> 00:02:52.890
- [Shelia] From there,
people get on the bus,

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.580
we'll give them their homework packets,

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:55.730
and they do their work.

00:02:56.621 --> 00:02:58.563
- Subtract that number and
then you get the number.

00:02:58.563 --> 00:02:59.396
- [John] Exactly, you
subtract that number.

00:02:59.396 --> 00:03:01.300
- Yeah, and then you get
the answer that you want.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.700
You know if I have a problem,
I'm calling you, right?

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.533
- Yeah.

00:03:04.533 --> 00:03:05.450
Let me show you a couple
more things though

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.690
before we start.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.276
- We started operating a few years ago

00:03:09.276 --> 00:03:11.373
and ever since then,
we have a lot of people

00:03:11.373 --> 00:03:12.880
that come on the bus.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.910
Give me some love.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.640
- Hi, baby.
- Hi honey.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.100
- I guess you could call it
like an education desert.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.800
There's not the facilities;
there's not the infrastructure,

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.180
and it's difficult for students to get

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.420
to where there are classrooms,

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.230
so it was designed with that in mind.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.370
And the fact that the bus is unique,

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.450
there's a sense of pride with that

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.640
that OK, this is maybe a community

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.270
that has been historically underserved

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.670
but now, we have something
that no one else has.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.340
- We serve everyone from
different walks of life,

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:46.430
we have people that's
working, that's not working,

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:50.103
we have people from age
16 to 116, doesn't matter.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.710
Some people come with their kids,

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.350
some people come straight from work,

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.280
some people come before
they have to go to work,

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.450
they put a lot of time and effort in

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.858
'cause they really want their education.

00:04:02.858 --> 00:04:05.215
(knocks)

00:04:05.215 --> 00:04:06.548
Hi, it's Shelia.

00:04:07.996 --> 00:04:08.829
Hi honey.

00:04:08.829 --> 00:04:10.810
My role on this bus is to go out

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.620
to the different neighborhoods and knock

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:13.700
on people's doors.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.276
I'll go wherever they need me to be,

00:04:15.276 --> 00:04:17.270
'cause I'm that person
that tries to get them in

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:18.933
and try to keep them in.

00:04:18.933 --> 00:04:21.138
Hi, how you doing, I'm
going to give you this,

00:04:21.138 --> 00:04:22.295
it's about Five Keys.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:23.378
If you know anybody that need a GED

00:04:23.378 --> 00:04:27.700
or high school diploma, right
there, that big green bus.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.533
Totally free.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.870
I'll call them; I'll bug them;

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.950
I'll text them; I'll email
them, whatever it takes.

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:37.870
I just want you to get
your education, that's it.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:40.035
I didn't even know how
to read a book to my son,

00:04:40.035 --> 00:04:42.320
and I got four kids, my oldest is 30.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:44.410
I let them know my story
like I couldn't read,

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.740
so don't be ashamed that you can't read,

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.120
that you can't do math,
that you dropped out

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.870
in fifth, sixth grade, it doesn't matter,

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.633
just come on back and we got you.

00:04:54.633 --> 00:04:56.401
I can show you, better, I can tell you.

00:04:56.401 --> 00:04:57.234
- [Man] OK.

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.163
- OK, nice meeting you guys.
- You too.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.760
- See you on Thursday.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:00.893
You too, God bless.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.620
- It be hard in the morning getting up,

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.510
but guess what?

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.860
It's worth it, because
you come here to learn

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.923
things that you never
learned or never knew.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.630
It's an encouraging
thing, it's like you know,

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.080
I'm getting ready, it's
like I'm going to school,

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:29.260
I feel like a big kid,
it's like, you know?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.640
- So I have a total of 20 squares.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.120
- I dropped out of school
in the sixth grade.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.983
Since then, it has been
one heck of a ride.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.170
I always have some excuse
as to why I couldn't

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:46.070
get it done, but it wasn't no excuse.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.960
Now we're working on algebra
and I'm looking forward

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.863
to graduating at the next graduation.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.760
- This bus has impacted hundreds of lives

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.410
in these different neighborhoods.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.083
It makes me happy to see a mother

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:06.776
or a father come on
this bus with their kids

00:06:06.776 --> 00:06:08.083
and push through.

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.080
I don't want them to feel like we're just

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.450
another program that
came in the neighborhood

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:17.540
and now we're gone, because we're here;

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.830
we're here to stay, so
that's why I keep going

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.820
'cause I want them to
know that we're real.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:22.653
Four.
- Yeah!

00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:25.327
- Yay, high five, ah.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.770
God gave me a second chance,

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:33.320
and I wanna show people that they

00:06:33.320 --> 00:06:34.720
can get a second chance too.

